description:
JMAP-h47t.17 added per-handler '`args` is the RFC 8620 §5.x ... request shape ... returned `Value` is the §5.x response shape' rustdoc to all 14 `handle_*` fns in jmap-tasks-server, plus a module-level 'Wire-shape contract' section in each of task.rs, task_list.rs, task_notification.rs. These docs close the contract gap that the bead flagged: a consumer reading docs.rs no longer needs to read RFC 8620 prose to know what to pass to `handle_task_get(args)`.

This is a divergence from the canonical sibling jmap-mail-server, which today carries only the short 'Returns (response_args, extra_invocations). The extra list is always empty.' trailer on most (not all) handlers and no module-level wire-shape contract section. Per the workspace canonical-template propagation rule, the same docstring shape MUST be propagated to:

1. jmap-mail-server (canonical) — every `handle_*` fn in src/email.rs, src/mailbox.rs, src/identity.rs, src/email_submission.rs, src/vacation.rs, src/search_snippet.rs, src/thread.rs, etc. Plus module-level Wire-shape contract sections.
2. jmap-chat-server — every `handle_*` fn in src/chat.rs, src/message.rs, src/space.rs, src/read_position.rs.
3. jmap-calendars-server — every `handle_*` fn (Calendar, CalendarEvent, ParticipantIdentity).
4. jmap-contacts-server — every `handle_*` fn.
5. jmap-filenode-server, jmap-metadata-server, jmap-sharing-server — similarly.

Pattern to follow (extracted from this commit):

  /// Handle an `Email/get` method call (RFC 8621 §5.1).
  ///
  /// `args` is the RFC 8620 §5.1 `/get` request shape (`accountId`, optional
  /// `ids`, optional `properties`); the returned `Value` is the §5.1
  /// `/get` response shape (`accountId`, `state`, `list`, `notFound`).
  ///
  /// (optional: type-specific notes, e.g. utcStart/utcDue augmentation on Task/get)
  ///
  /// Returns `(response_args, extra_invocations)`. The extra list is always empty.

Plus a module-level paragraph in each .rs file:

  //! # Wire-shape contract
  //!
  //! Every `handle_*` function in this module conforms to the canonical JMAP
  //! method shape. The `args: serde_json::Value` parameter MUST be a JSON
  //! Object whose fields match the corresponding RFC 8620 §5 method shape
  //! ... (cite the spec sections relevant to the module)
  //!
  //! Returns `(Value, Vec<Invocation>)`. Extra invocations are populated ...
  //! Each handler returns `Err(JmapError)` for method-level failures ...
  //! Per-target failures inside `/set` surface in `notCreated`/`notUpdated`/`notDestroyed`.

The mail-server _changes handlers (handle_email_changes, handle_mailbox_changes, etc.) are MISSING the 'Returns ...' trailer that the other handlers have — this is pre-existing canonical drift that the sweep should fix.

Rationale: docs.rs is the contract surface for downstream consumers; a minimal one-line spec citation is not enough to know what to pass. The bead-author's specific concern was 'callers must read RFC 8620 prose to know what to pass'; per-handler wire-shape rustdoc is the lowest-cost workspace-canonical fix.

No API break. Pure docs. Can land as one large mechanical pass.

Cross-reference: JMAP-h47t.17 (closed in this commit) is the tasks-server-local instance of this sweep. Was originally human-labeled, ratified after 72h stale recommendation per workspace AGENTS.md 'When NOT to file human' anti-pattern.
